                        "name": "Jae Hyun Yoo",
                        "email": "jae.yoo@oss.qualcomm.com",
                        "username": "jaehyoo"
                    },
                    "message": "I think this is a somewhat risky assumption.  If another BMC SoC is added in the future, anything without soc0/family would automatically be identified as Nuvoton.  We should probably make this logic more robust.  Could it be improved using /sys/firmware/devicetree/base/compatible instead?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "create_usbhid.sh",
                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Hariharan Rangasamy",
                        "email": "hariharanr@ami.com",
                        "username": "hariharanrangasamy"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "create_usbhid.sh",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jae Hyun Yoo",
                        "email": "jae.yoo@oss.qualcomm.com",
                        "username": "jaehyoo"
                    },
                    "message": "It's repeating 3 points in this script. Would it be better if we set a variable here so that in other points can use the variable to determine how to connect and disconnect it?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "create_usbhid.sh",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Hariharan Rangasamy",
                        "email": "hariharanr@ami.com",
                        "username": "hariharanrangasamy"
                    },
                    "message": "Added AST25XX_DEV_NAME, AST27XX_DEV_NAME, NPCM_DEV_NAME for dev names"
                },
                {
                    "file": "create_usbhid.sh",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jae Hyun Yoo",
                        "email": "jae.yoo@oss.qualcomm.com",
                        "username": "jaehyoo"
                    },
                    "message": "This is an error case, so might it better to output the message to stderr using >&2 ?"
                },
                {
